From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: natemu <natemu@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEXCore: slice1 I9 addendum: CVTPI2PS m64 MMX transition

Under fexc_slice1, CVTPI2PS xmm, m64 makes the x87-to-MMX transition
(TOP = 0, every tag valid) as its register form does: the SDM's
CVTPI2PS page gives the transition for both operand forms (CVTPI2PD
xmm, m64 is the form that makes none). FEX made it only when an
operand was an MMX register.
---
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/Vector.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/Vector.cpp
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/Vector.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/Vector.cpp
@@ -406,6 +406,11 @@
 }
 
 void OpDispatchBuilder::InsertMMX_To_XMM_Vector_CVT_Int_To_Float(OpcodeArgs) {
+  // natemu slice1 (I9 addendum): CVTPI2PS makes the x87-to-MMX transition (TOP = 0, every tag valid) with a memory source too
+  // (SDM CVTPI2PS: no operand exception; CVTPI2PD xmm, m64 is the form that does not); the register source made it already.
+  if (fexc_slice1 && MMXState == MMXState_X87) {
+    ChgStateX87_MMX();
+  }
   // We load the full vector width when dealing with a source vector,
   // so that we don't do any unnecessary zero extension to the scalar
   // element that we're going to operate on.
-- 
